+// --- fdlibm's software square root (most GameCube / Wii games) ---------------------------------
+// CodeWarrior's MSL math library computes sqrt() with fdlibm's __ieee754_sqrt: bit by bit, ~54
+// loop passes, well over a thousand emulated instructions per call (the Gekko has no exact
+// square-root instruction). Crash of the Titans spends ~6.5% of its CPU thread there. The result
+// is the correctly rounded square root, which the host's sqrtsd gives directly (round to nearest,
+// no flush-to-zero: the library's own rounding step folds to nearest). Found by its code in any
+// game's memory; only the errno and NaN-constant addresses differ between games.
